export anchor DesertStarsStyle:
    number: 420
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Desert stars
    idea: The trip under a desert night sky, a full width starfield that warms to an ember horizon over dune silhouettes, a huge thin title, the route drawn as a three star constellation, the itinerary as a glowing star line, and the weather sitting on the horizon.
    base: dark
    palette:
        sky: #0b0d24, the upper night sky behind the hero
        deep: #070818, the zenith at the top of the sky gradient
        panel: #0c0e28, the itinerary glass panel at 82 percent
        ground: #120c16, dunes, the lower band and the page below
        duneCard: #1a1220, style sheet cards, fields and list rows
        ink: #f6efe4, text
        muted: #b9b3d1, captions, labels and Not booked
        star: #fff6d8, stars, nodes, the constellation and focus
        ember: #ffb37a, the horizon glow, dates and the primary button
        onEmber: #2a1206, text on ember
        rose: #f5a8bb, the cherry blossom note and the meter start
        gold: #ffe08a, Booked and Done stars
    type:
        Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial. Base 16px
        at 1.6. The title 88px at 200 on two lines, the horizon figure 96px
        at 200 in star white, leg titles 22px at 300, labels 13px caps
        tracked 0.3em, dates 12px caps tracked 0.2em in ember.
    layout:
        A full width night hero. The sky runs from near black at the top
        through indigo to a plum and ember band at the horizon, scattered
        with small stars, and two dune silhouettes close it at the bottom.
        Over it a quiet top row with a star and BRIGHTWORK TRIPS in spaced
        caps and the dates on the right. Then two columns. On the left Mara
        Okafor and one guest in ember caps, Japan in April as a huge thin
        title, and below it the route as a constellation, three haloed stars
        named Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka in spaced caps joined by fine lines,
        with an italic caption. On the right a 28px rounded glass panel
        holds Itinerary as a vertical star line. Each leg has a node on the
        line, glowing solid when booked, a dashed ring when not, small for
        flights, then the date in ember, the title, the detail and a status
        at the right. Two pill buttons end the panel. On the horizon itself
        sits 17 degrees in a huge glowing figure beside a dark chip with the
        weather sentence and the blossom note. Below the dunes, on the
        ground colour, two quiet blocks under thin rules, Before the journey
        with star bullets and Budget with a 56px thin 3,200 and a rose to
        ember glowing line. Below 900px the columns stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit with very wide gaps. 64px between title and panel and 120px of horizon below the weather.
    density: Low. One title, one constellation, one list, a horizon figure and two quiet blocks.
    corners: A 28px glass panel, and pill buttons, fields and rows.
    borders: A faint star coloured edge on the glass panel and a thin vertical star line through the itinerary.
    shadows: No drop shadows. Stars, nodes, the meter and the horizon figure glow.
    icons:
        Stars as states. Booked and Done are a filled gold star, Not booked
        and To do a dashed hollow star and Flight a thin plane. Booked nodes
        glow and unbooked nodes are dashed rings.
    focus: A 2px star white outline offset 4px with a soft halo.
    tone: Hushed and poetic, such as Before the journey and The route read like a constellation.
